IMPORT prelude

-- Casino Control Act 2006 (Singapore) -- family exclusion orders, start to finish: who decides (ss 157, 158), who may apply
-- (ss 2 "family member", 159 to 161), the grounds (s 162), the terms (s 163), the family visit limit as the milder alternative
-- (s 163A), provisional orders (s 164), orders made in the respondent's absence (s 165C), variation and revocation (ss 166,
-- 166A), service (s 167), and the effect on the respondent and the casino (ss 125 to 128, 195).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 21 September 2026, with Act 29 of 2024), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CCA2006.txt. Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit. The deposit's table of
-- contents is misaligned by one line in this Subdivision (it prints "159. Application by or on behalf of person below 21" and
-- "163A. Provisional family exclusion order"); in the body, s 159 is the application, s 160 the under-21 rule, s 161 the
-- incapacitated applicant, s 162 the grounds, s 163 the terms, s 163A the family visit limit and s 164 the provisional order.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0271 (Jun Hao scenario, event j081): a sister applies for a family exclusion order against
-- her brother, who gambles at the casino on paydays. Who may apply, on what grounds, and who decides?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: third party exclusion orders and visit limits (s 165); persons excluded by law (s 165A); self-exclusion and
-- voluntary visit limits (ss 165AA, 165B); the visit-count mechanics of a visit limit (s 165D); the list of excluded persons
-- beyond its existence (s 168); secrecy (s 169); the Rules (s 170) -- the "prescribed time" for setting aside an absence order
-- is in them and was not retrieved; the Council's own constitution and quorum (ss 154 to 156A); the Committee's evidence-gathering
-- powers (s 158(4), (5)); the Authority's and Commissioner of Police's exclusion orders (ss 121 to 123).
-- The cruder s 162 test in cca-patrons.l4 is left as it was; this module stands alone and imports nothing from it.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules approach. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md. Lines marked INFERENCE are the encoder's reading, not the Act's words.

§ `Casino Control Act 2006 -- family exclusion orders`

§§ `2 -- family member`

-- s 2(1): "family member", in relation to a respondent, means -- (a) a spouse of the respondent; (b) a child of the respondent,
-- including an adopted child and a stepchild; (c) a parent of the respondent, including an adoptive parent and a step-parent; and
-- (d) a sibling of the respondent, including an adoptive sibling, a stepsibling and a half-sibling.
--
-- The list is closed ("means"). A sibling qualifies with no further condition: no age, no co-residence, no dependency.
-- Grandparents, grandchildren, in-laws, aunts, uncles, cousins and former spouses are not family members for this Part.
DECLARE Relationship IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `child`
    `adopted child`
    `stepchild`
    `parent`
    `adoptive parent`
    `step-parent`
    `sibling`
    `adoptive sibling`
    `stepsibling`
    `half-sibling`
    `grandparent`
    `grandchild`
    `parent-in-law`
    `sibling-in-law`
    `aunt or uncle`
    `niece or nephew`
    `cousin`
    `former spouse`
    `friend or unrelated person`

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A Relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a family member under s 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adopted child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `stepchild` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adoptive parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `step-parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sibling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adoptive sibling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `stepsibling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `half-sibling` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `157, 158 -- who decides`

-- s 159(2): "An application must be made to the Council in writing in the form approved by the Council, and the Council must refer
-- the application to a Committee." s 158(1): "A Committee must consider and determine in accordance with this Part all applications
-- for family exclusion orders or family visit limits referred to the Committee". s 157(1): the chairperson of the Council "must,
-- from time to time, constitute a Committee of Assessors consisting of -- (a) a chairperson, being a member of the Council or a
-- special affiliate; and (b) 2 other members selected from the panel of assessors". The Council is the National Council on Problem
-- Gambling (s 154). s 166(1): "The Council may confirm, vary or revoke" a family exclusion order. s 165C(4): "A Committee may
-- determine an application to set aside" an order made in the respondent's absence.
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `the National Council on Problem Gambling`
    `a Committee of Assessors`
    `the Minister`
    `the Casino Regulatory Authority`
    `a court`

DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `receiving the application`
    `deciding the application`
    `making a provisional order`
    `setting aside an order made in the respondent's absence`
    `varying or revoking the order`
    `substituting a family visit limit for the order`
    `keeping the list of excluded persons`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A Body
`who acts at` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `receiving the application` THEN `the National Council on Problem Gambling`
    WHEN `deciding the application` THEN `a Committee of Assessors`
    WHEN `making a provisional order` THEN `a Committee of Assessors`
    WHEN `setting aside an order made in the respondent's absence` THEN `a Committee of Assessors`
    OTHERWISE `the National Council on Problem Gambling`

GIVEN `the chair is a Council member or special affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN, `members from the panel` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee is constituted as s 157 requires` IF
    `the chair is a Council member or special affiliate` AND `members from the panel` EQUALS 2

-- s 158(2): before any determination against a person the Committee "must, by a written notice, give the person a reasonable
-- opportunity to object". (3): "No party to any proceedings before a Committee may be represented by an advocate and solicitor"
-- except the person making the application on behalf of an applicant under s 160 or 161. (6): questions of fact on "a balance of
-- probabilities". (7): not bound by the strict rules of evidence.
GIVEN `the lawyer is applying on the applicant's behalf under s 160 or 161` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a lawyer may appear before the Committee` IF
    `the lawyer is applying on the applicant's behalf under s 160 or 161`

§§ `159 to 161 -- who may apply`

-- s 159(1): "An application for a family exclusion order against a respondent may be made by -- (a) a family member of the
-- respondent adversely affected by the respondent's gambling; or (b) a person referred to in section 160 or 161 on behalf of a
-- family member referred to in paragraph (a)."
-- s 160: if the person "is below 21 years of age", the application may be made "(a) by the person, with the permission of the
-- Council, if the person is at least 16 years of age; or (b) on behalf of the person by -- (i) a parent or guardian of the
-- person; or (ii) with the permission of the Council, any other family member or other relative of the person."
-- s 161: where a person "is unable to make an application (whether by reason of physical or mental infirmity or for any other
-- reason)", it may be made on the person's behalf "(a) with the permission of the Council, by any family member or other relative
-- of the person; or (b) by any person appointed by the Minister."
--
-- So the person who must be the respondent's family member, and adversely affected, is the person FOR WHOM the application is
-- made; the person who files it may be someone else only through s 160 or 161.
DECLARE `Who files` IS ONE OF
    `the affected family member personally`
    `a parent or guardian of the affected family member`
    `another family member or relative of the affected family member`
    `a person appointed by the Minister`

DECLARE `Affected person` HAS
    `relationship to the respondent` IS A Relationship
    `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to be adversely affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `able to make an application` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS AN `Affected person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may benefit from an application for a family exclusion order` IF
        `is a family member under s 2` (`the person`'s `relationship to the respondent`)
    AND `the person`'s `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling`

-- INFERENCE: s 160(b)(i) lets a parent or guardian file for a person under 21 without permission. For an incapacitated adult the
-- parent files under s 161(a) as a "family member or other relative", which needs the Council's permission. A guardian who is not a
-- relative cannot file for an incapacitated adult except by appointment by the Minister.
GIVEN `the person` IS AN `Affected person`, `the filer` IS A `Who files`, `the Council has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the filer may file under ss 159 to 161` IF
    CONSIDER `the filer`
    WHEN `the affected family member personally` THEN
            `the person`'s `able to make an application`
        AND (   `the person`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 21
             OR (`the person`'s `age in years` AT LEAST 16 AND `the Council has given permission`))
    WHEN `a parent or guardian of the affected family member` THEN
            `the person`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 21
        OR ((NOT `the person`'s `able to make an application`) AND `the Council has given permission`)
    WHEN `another family member or relative of the affected family member` THEN
            `the Council has given permission`
        AND (`the person`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 21 OR (NOT `the person`'s `able to make an application`))
    WHEN `a person appointed by the Minister` THEN
        NOT `the person`'s `able to make an application`

GIVEN `the person` IS AN `Affected person`, `the filer` IS A `Who files`, `the Council has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a family exclusion order application may be made` IF
        `may benefit from an application for a family exclusion order` `the person`
    AND `the filer may file under ss 159 to 161` `the person` `the filer` `the Council has given permission`

§§ `163A -- the family visit limit, a wider door`

-- s 163A(1): an application for a family visit limit may be made by "(a) a family member of the respondent who is, or is likely to
-- be, adversely affected by the respondent's gambling". A family member not yet affected can apply for a visit limit but not for an
-- exclusion order. (4): the Committee may make it if satisfied "(a) there is a reasonable apprehension that the respondent has
-- engaged, or is likely to engage, in gambling activities irresponsibly, without due regard to the needs and welfare of the
-- respondent's family members; (b) a family visit limit ... is appropriate ...; (c) subject to section 165C, the respondent has been
-- given an opportunity to object ...; and (d) it would be in the best interests of the respondent and his or her family members".
-- (5): it must specify the period and "the maximum number of visits in aggregate that the respondent may make to any casino in each
-- month". There is no three-month test.
GIVEN `the person` IS AN `Affected person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may benefit from an application for a family visit limit` IF
        `is a family member under s 2` (`the person`'s `relationship to the respondent`)
    AND (`the person`'s `adversely affected by the respondent's gambling` OR `the person`'s `likely to be adversely affected`)

§§ `162 -- the grounds`

-- s 162(1): "the Committee may make a family exclusion order against a respondent if the Committee is satisfied that -- (a) there is
-- a reasonable apprehension that the respondent may cause serious harm to family members because of his or her gambling; (b) the
-- making of the order is appropriate in the circumstances; (c) subject to section 165C, the respondent has been given an
-- opportunity to object to the application; and (d) it would be in the best interests of the respondent and his or her family
-- members to make the order."
-- (2): serious harm if the respondent "(a) has engaged in gambling activities irresponsibly, without due regard to the needs and
-- welfare of the respondent's family members; and (b) has done so repeatedly over a period of not less than 3 months or in a
-- particularly irresponsible manner over a lesser period."
-- (3): reasonable apprehension if "(a) the respondent has caused such harm prior to the complaint, according to the test set out in
-- subsection (2); and (b) there is reason to believe that the respondent's irresponsible gambling behaviour will continue or recur."
-- (4): events outside Singapore may be taken into account. (5): if the respondent consents, the order may be made "without
-- receiving any further submission or evidence as to the grounds". (6): an application may be dismissed at any stage as "frivolous,
-- vexatious, without substance or has no reasonable prospect of success".
--
-- "Gambling" (s 2) is "gambling whether or not inside casino premises, and includes remote gambling". Paydays at the casino count;
-- so would a betting app.
DECLARE `Family exclusion facts` HAS
    `gambled irresponsibly without regard to the family's needs and welfare` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months over which it was repeated` IS A NUMBER
    `particularly irresponsible over a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reason to believe it will continue or recur` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order is appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `respondent given the s 158(2) notice and an opportunity to object` IS A BOOLEAN
    `absence order conditions in s 165C(1) met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the best interests of the respondent and the family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respondent consents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `frivolous, vexatious, without substance or hopeless` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Family exclusion facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serious harm under s 162(2)` IF
        `the facts`'s `gambled irresponsibly without regard to the family's needs and welfare`
    AND (`the facts`'s `months over which it was repeated` AT LEAST 3 OR `the facts`'s `particularly irresponsible over a shorter period`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Family exclusion facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reasonable apprehension under s 162(3)` IF
    `serious harm under s 162(2)` `the facts` AND `the facts`'s `reason to believe it will continue or recur`

-- s 162(1)(c) "subject to section 165C": the opportunity to object is not needed where s 165C(1) lets the order be made in absence
-- (the respondent ignored the notice or summons, said he would not respond, or could not be found or is outside Singapore).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Family exclusion facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hearing requirement is met` IF
    `the facts`'s `respondent given the s 158(2) notice and an opportunity to object` OR `the facts`'s `absence order conditions in s 165C(1) met`

-- INFERENCE on s 162(5): consent dispenses with "submission or evidence as to the grounds", so the encoding treats consent as
-- standing in for (a), (b) and (d); a consenting respondent has necessarily had the opportunity to object. The Committee still
-- "may", not "must".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Family exclusion facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee may make a family exclusion order` IF
        (NOT `the facts`'s `frivolous, vexatious, without substance or hopeless`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the respondent consents`
         OR (    `a reasonable apprehension under s 162(3)` `the facts`
             AND `the facts`'s `the order is appropriate in the circumstances`
             AND `the hearing requirement is met` `the facts`
             AND `the facts`'s `in the best interests of the respondent and the family`))

§§ `163 -- the terms`

-- s 163(1): a family exclusion order "(a) must specify the period during which it is in force; and (b) may apply for the benefit of
-- all of the respondent's family members or specified family members." No minimum or maximum period is set by the Act.
-- (2): "Without limiting the matters that may be the subject of a family exclusion order, an order may do one or more of the
-- following: (a) refer the respondent to participate in a programme of counselling, rehabilitation or special education ...; (b) ban
-- the respondent from -- (i) entering or remaining on all casino premises; or (ii) taking part in any casino gambling or promotional
-- game on all casino premises; (c) require the respondent to close any deposit account in a casino; (d) require a casino operator to
-- close any deposit account of the respondent with the casino; (e) ban the respondent from ... gaming machine rooms ...; (f) ban the
-- respondent from engaging in all manner of general remote gambling; (g) impose all ... or any combination".
-- s 164(2): a provisional order "may do one or more things mentioned in section 163(2)" -- for a provisional order the list is closed.
DECLARE Measure IS ONE OF
    `refer to counselling, rehabilitation or special education`
    `ban entering or remaining on all casino premises`
    `ban casino gambling and promotional games`
    `respondent to close casino deposit accounts`
    `casino operator to close the respondent's deposit accounts`
    `ban gaming machine rooms`
    `ban general remote gambling`
    `cap monthly casino visits`
    `fine the respondent`
    `garnish the respondent's wages`

GIVEN `the measure` IS A Measure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is listed in s 163(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the measure`
    WHEN `cap monthly casino visits` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `fine the respondent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `garnish the respondent's wages` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the measure` IS A Measure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provisional order may impose` IF
    `is listed in s 163(2)` `the measure`

GIVEN `a period is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order meets s 163(1)(a)` IF
    `a period is specified`

§§ `164 -- provisional family exclusion orders`

-- s 164(1): "Where, upon an application for a family exclusion order under section 159, a Committee is satisfied that the
-- respondent has caused serious harm to family members having regard to section 162(2) and further harm to family members is
-- imminent, the Committee may make a provisional family exclusion order, even though the application under section 159 has not been
-- determined."
-- (2): it "takes effect on the date on which [it] is served on the respondent or such later date as the Committee may specify", and
-- "ceases to have effect on the first occurrence of" -- (a) withdrawal of the application; (b) (i) dismissal, or (ii) the family
-- exclusion order taking effect; (c) if the application is not determined before the 28th day after the making of the provisional
-- order, "upon the 28th day ... or such later date as the Committee may determine in any particular case".
--
-- s 164 does not mention an opportunity to object; a provisional order can be made before the respondent is heard.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Family exclusion facts`, `further harm is imminent` IS A BOOLEAN, `the application is undetermined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee may make a provisional order` IF
    `serious harm under s 162(2)` `the facts` AND `further harm is imminent` AND `the application is undetermined`

GIVEN `later day fixed by the Committee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the provisional order lapses` MEANS
    IF `later day fixed by the Committee` GREATER THAN 28 THEN `later day fixed by the Committee` ELSE 28

GIVEN `served on the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since it was made` IS A NUMBER,
      `later day fixed by the Committee` IS A NUMBER,
      `application withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `application dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the family exclusion order has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisional order is in effect` IF
        `served on the respondent`
    AND (NOT `application withdrawn`)
    AND (NOT `application dismissed`)
    AND (NOT `the family exclusion order has taken effect`)
    AND `days since it was made` LESS THAN `the day the provisional order lapses` `later day fixed by the Committee`

§§ `165C, 166, 166A -- challenge, variation and revocation`

-- No appeal lies against a family exclusion order. The only appeal in Division 3 is s 165(10), for THIRD PARTY orders, "to the
-- Council whose decision is final". (INFERENCE: no appeal to a court is provided; judicial review is outside the Act and not
-- encoded.)
-- s 165C(3): an order made in the respondent's absence may be set aside "on the application of the respondent within the prescribed
-- time and in the prescribed manner"; (4) the Committee may confirm, vary or set it aside.
-- s 166(1): "The Council may confirm, vary or revoke -- (a) a family exclusion order ... on an application by -- (i) a family member
-- for whose benefit the family exclusion order ... was made; or (ii) the respondent". (2): the respondent needs "the permission of
-- the Council and permission is only to be granted if the Council is satisfied that there has been a substantial change in the
-- relevant circumstances since the order ... was made or last varied". (2A)(d): the Council may instead substitute a family visit
-- limit (s 166A(2)(a)). (4): both the respondent and the beneficiary family member must be allowed to make representations. (5): the
-- decision "is final"; (6) but a fresh application may be made later.
GIVEN `the order was made in the respondent's absence` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the respondent may apply to set the order aside` IF
    `the order was made in the respondent's absence` AND `within the prescribed time`

GIVEN `is a family member for whose benefit the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `substantial change since the order was made or last varied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may entertain an application to vary or revoke` IF
        `is a family member for whose benefit the order was made`
    OR (`is the respondent` AND `substantial change since the order was made or last varied`)

GIVEN `the order is a family exclusion order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies under the Act against the order` IF
    NOT `the order is a family exclusion order`

§§ `167, 125 to 128, 195 -- effect`

-- s 167(1): except where made under s 165C(1)(c) (respondent cannot be found or is outside Singapore), an order "must be served on
-- the respondent and is not binding on the person named in the order ... until it has been so served". s 168(1)(a): the respondent
-- goes on the list of excluded persons. s 2: a "casino-excluded person" is one banned from entering or remaining on, or taking part
-- in gambling on, casino premises under, among others, "a family exclusion order, provisional family exclusion order or third party
-- exclusion order under Part 10".
-- s 125(1): a casino-excluded person "who knows, or ought reasonably to know, that he or she is a casino-excluded person, must not --
-- (a) enter or remain on; or (b) take part in any casino gambling or promotional game on, any casino premises". (2): an offence.
-- INFERENCE: s 125 sets no penalty, so the general penalty in s 195(2) applies -- a fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 12
-- months or both.
-- s 126(1): the operator "must not, without reasonable excuse, permit a casino-excluded person to enter or remain"; (2)(c) must close
-- the deposit accounts on being given an order under s 163(2)(d); (3) failure means disciplinary action (not an offence).
-- s 128(2): winnings of an excluded person who enters in contravention "are forfeited to the Consolidated Fund".
GIVEN `the order bans casino entry or casino gambling` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `served on the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made in absence because the respondent could not be found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the respondent is a casino-excluded person` IF
        `the order bans casino entry or casino gambling`
    AND (`served on the respondent` OR `made in absence because the respondent could not be found`)

GIVEN `is casino-excluded` IS A BOOLEAN, `knows or ought reasonably to know` IS A BOOLEAN, `entered casino premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the respondent commits the s 125 offence` IF
    `is casino-excluded` AND `knows or ought reasonably to know` AND `entered casino premises`

`the maximum fine for the s 125 offence` MEANS 10000
`the maximum imprisonment in months for the s 125 offence` MEANS 12

GIVEN `is casino-excluded` IS A BOOLEAN, `entered casino premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the respondent's winnings are forfeited` IF
    `is casino-excluded` AND `entered casino premises`

GIVEN `is casino-excluded` IS A BOOLEAN, `the operator let the respondent in` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator is liable to disciplinary action under s 126` IF
    `is casino-excluded` AND `the operator let the respondent in` AND (NOT `reasonable excuse`)
